        "text": "I'll analyze the Texas lobbying statute to answer questions about the principal's (employer's) periodic spending report. \n\nKey observation: Texas Chapter 305 imposes registration and reporting obligations on the **registrant/lobbyist** (Section 305.005, 305.006), not separately on the principal/employer. There is no separate \"principal's spending report\" required under this chapter. However, Section 305.005(f)(3) and (f)(6) require the registrant to disclose information about the persons who employ/retain them. I'll answer based on what the statute requires regarding employer/principal disclosures within the registrant's reporting framework.\n\nGiven there's no separate principal spending report, most binary answers about its contents would be false. Let me record these carefully.",
